        "original_id": "b53e48d2-62e0-5f71-8635-291b31cdcd99",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: First Silesian War, Silesian Wars\n- People: Frederick the Great, Frederick II, Maria Theresa\n- Places: Prussia, Austria\n- Roles: King of Prussia, Hohenzollern king\n\nFacts:\n- The First Silesian War became the first of three Silesian Wars fought between Frederick the Great's Prussia and Maria Theresa's Austria.\n- Frederick II, also known as Frederick the Great, was born on 24 January 1712 and died on 17 August 1786.\n- Frederick II was King of Prussia from 1740 until 1786.\n- Frederick II had the longest reign of any Hohenzollern king.",
